 "coupling_convention": "d_e (dimensionless)",
 "notes": "Fermilab Holometer twin-interferometer cross-correlation search for scalar-field DM (1.6e-12 to 1.0e-7 eV). Curve traced from the vector figure gammaC_scalar.pdf in the arXiv e-print (Fig. 2 top-right: photon coupling Lambda_gamma^-1 [GeV^-1] vs m_phi, Basic Scalar scenario with standard halo rho=0.4 GeV/cm^3; the Dilaton/Modulus scenario gives the identical Holometer curve, the Relaxion Halo scenario was not used). Axis calibration from gridline paths (x: 1e-15..1e-5 eV, y: 1e-25..1e-5 GeV^-1), verified against the paper's quoted mass endpoints. Converted to Damour-Donoghue d_e via alpha->alpha(1+phi/Lambda_gamma) = alpha(1+d_e kappa phi), i.e. d_e = Lambda_gamma^-1 x M_Pl/sqrt(4pi) = 3.4416e18 GeV x Lambda_gamma^-1. Raw polyline (1355 vertices) resampled to 200 log-uniform mass points; very narrow resonance spikes (up and down, incl. segments clipped at the plot ceiling Lambda_gamma^-1=1e-5) are partially smoothed by resampling. Paper also constrains the electron coupling Lambda_e (Fig. 2 left column), not reported here. 95% CL.",
